Fix two field definitions in ST's STM32MP2 CMSIS headers (STM32CubeMP2 v1.3.2), every
CM33 and CM0 variant:

- RTC_HWCFGR_RIF is bits 31:28, as its own mask comment (0xF0000000) says; the header
  puts it at bit 24, on top of TRUST_ZONE. TAMP_HWCFGR2 has the same RIF-above-
  TRUST_ZONE nibble pair at the right offsets.
- TAMP_HWCFGR1_INT_TAMPER is bits 31:16, as its mask comment (0xFFFF0000) says and as
  the STM32U5 TAMP_HWCFGR1 lays it out; the header defines it at bit 8 with
  ACTIVE_TAMPER's position and mask, on top of TAMPER and ACTIVE_TAMPER.

Without this the parsed IR has overlapping fields, which `chiptool check` rejects.

